# Agent deliverables → local `Cursor output/`

This repo is the user's local **Vibe Coding Area** folder. All agents (Cloud Agent, IDE Agent, subagents) must sync user-facing outputs into the repo so they appear after git pull/merge on the user's machine.

## Required output location

- Put **all deliverable outputs** under repo-root `Cursor output/` (create it if missing).
- Examples: notes, summaries, Q&A knowledge bases, reports, CSVs, charts, exports, checklists, walkthrough docs meant for the user to reopen later.
- Prefer a clear subfolder by topic, e.g.:
  - `Cursor output/YouTube知識筆記/`
  - `Cursor output/報告/`
  - `Cursor output/<project-or-topic>/`
- Use descriptive filenames (date or source id when helpful).

## Do not

- Do not leave deliverables only in chat.
- Do not put user deliverables only under `/tmp`, `/opt/cursor/artifacts`, or other ephemeral paths without also copying the final files into `Cursor output/`.
- Do not scatter one-off notes across random project folders unless the user asked for a specific project path.

## Git sync (so local folder sees them)

- Commit files under `Cursor output/` on the working branch and push, so the user's local clone can pull and open them in **Vibe Coding Area**.
- When updating an existing note, edit the file in `Cursor output/` rather than creating a disconnected copy.

## Scope exceptions

- Normal product/source code still goes in the relevant project directories (`Trading Bot/`, `Crypto Screener/`, etc.).
- This rule is about **agent-produced artifacts and knowledge the user wants to keep and reopen locally**.
